<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n39288" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπίδοξ-ος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>likely</i>, of persons,
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐ. γενέσθαι ἐπιεικεῖς</span>
			<i>likely</i> to turn out well, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Tht.</u>
				143d
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐ. τοῦτο</span>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πείσεσθαι</span>
			<i>in danger</i> of suffering . . , <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				6.12
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐ. ὢν πάσχειν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Antipho
					2.1.5
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				2.4.9
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐ. ὢν τυχεῖν</span> being
				<i>expected</i> to gain . . , <i><span class="en">
				Isoc.
				6.8
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τοὺς</span>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐ. γενήσεσθαι πονηρούς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					20.12
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπιδοξοτέρου ὄντος</span> (sc.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αἱρεθῆναι</span>) <i><span class="en">
				App.
				<u>BC</u>
				1.32
			</span></i>: sts. c. fut.
			part., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐ. ἦσαν ἐμβαλοῦντες</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plu.
					<u>Agis</u>
					13
				</span></i>
			; of things, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐ. ἡ ἀπόστασις παρασχίδων ὀστέων
					ἀπιέναι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hp.
					<u>Fract.</u>
					24
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐ</span>. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γενέσθαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hdt.
					1.89
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πρὸς οὓς ἐ. [ἐστι] πολεμεῖν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arist.
					<u>Rh.</u>
					1359b39
				</span></i>
			: abs., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὅσα . . κακὰ ἐπίδοξα
				καταλαμβάνειν </span>(<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-λαμβάνει</span> codd.) <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				4.11
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>. of repute,
				<i>glorious</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κῦδος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pi.
					<u>N.</u>
					9.46
				</span></i>
			; and in late Prose, as <i><span class="en">
				LXX
				<u>Si.</u>
				3.18
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				D.S.
				13.83
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				2.239d
			</span></i>, etc. Adv.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-ξως</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					LXX
					<u>1 Es.</u>
					9.45
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				<u>IG</u>
				12(7).117
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				288
			</span></i> (<span class="entity">Amorgos</span>), <i><span class="en">
				Artem.
				2.30
			</span></i>.</div>
